## Where do I put / find a figure?

The one question that decides everything: **can code regenerate it?**

- **Yes — a plot the pipeline makes from data** → it belongs in `results/figures/`.
  It is a *build target*: gitignored, regenerated on every run. **Never edit it by
  hand — your changes will be silently overwritten.** To change it, edit the
  plotting code in `src/` or a config in `conf/` and rerun.
- **No — a human drew it** (schematic, experimental design, BioRender export) →
  it belongs in `assets/figures/`. It is a *source input*: git-tracked, precious.
  Keep the editable source (`.svg`/`.ai`) next to any exported PDF.

**Composite plates** (schematic panel + generated panels): prefer assembling them
programmatically in a pipeline stage (reads `assets/` + `results/`, writes a new
plate to `results/figures/` — fully regenerable). If assembled by hand instead,
the plate becomes a source asset in `assets/figures/` and loses regenerability —
an acceptable trade for complex schematics, made deliberately.

Light vs dark: `results/figures/light/` is canonical (for print/papers);
`results/figures/dark/` is derived for on-screen slides (transparent background).
Both come from the same code and the theme in `conf/theme/`.

